; AmiBroker ASCII import format for CLOSE-ONLY series in the Banyu Langit export.
;
; Why a separate format: 34 of the GLOBAL series have no true Open/High/Low at the source.
; Every yield curve series (ID1M..ID30Y), every macro release (CPI, PMI, SRBI, GDP), plus
; COAL, TIN and RUBBER RSS3 only ever published a settlement/close price. custom_ohlc stores
; 0 in open/high/low for those rows.
;
; Feeding 0 into Open/High/Low is not a small blemish: every candle, moving average, ATR and
; backtest built on those bars would be wrong, while looking perfectly healthy. AmiBroker fills
; the missing fields from Close when the column is absent, so the fix is to omit them.
;
; $BREAKONERR 1 is deliberate, same reason as banyulangit.format: a rejected line must fail
; loudly instead of leaving a half-empty database that reports "ok".

$FORMAT Ticker,Date_YMD,Close
$SEPARATOR ,
$SKIPLINES 0
$AUTOADD 1
$BREAKONERR 1
$DEBUG 1
